# Working method

## Read

- Search to find the owner. Read a file whole when you will edit it or reason
  about its behaviour.
- One authority cluster per change and per PR. A wider audit needs the user's
  request.
- Open `docs/CANON.md` or `docs/DECISIONS.md` to add or change a law.
- Never read generated or duplicate context: `node_modules/`, `dist/`,
  `.claude/worktrees/`, `artifacts/`, `reference/*.txt`, `*.actual.png`,
  `*.diff.png`. Never print a bundle, an atlas or golden data.

## Delegate

- Delegate independent clusters in parallel, one worktree each. Brief each
  subagent with its file list, the method, and the check that proves its result.
- A comment-only pass proves itself with `npm run codehash`. A code move proves
  itself with `npm run lint` and the closest test.
- A subagent report is a claim. Read the diff before you merge it.

## Verify

- `npm run lint` after every code edit: undefined names, unused bindings, world
  stage wiring. It takes one second.
- Then the closest `npm run test:<area>`, a domain aggregate when a cluster
  changes, `npm test` once at handoff, `npm run verify` when the build or entry
  point changes. A broad pass supersedes its subsets.
- Repeat a level only after a relevant edit. Never suppress an assertion.
- Regenerate a baseline only after an intentional authority change, through its
  `*:update` script.

## Frames

- Measure first: a structural test or a derived number.
- Then look. Capture with `tools/shot.mjs` and read the PNG. A change to drawn
  output is unverified until its frame has been seen.
- `.cursor/rules/pixel-review-gate.mdc` owns who decides a subjective change.
